# 📂 GUI File Sorting Application

A Python-based GUI application that automatically organizes files into folders based on their extensions. Built using Tkinter for a simple and user-friendly interface.

---

## 🚀 Features

- 📁 Select any folder from your system
- ⚡ Automatically sorts files into categories:
  - Images
  - Videos
  - Audio
  - Documents
  - Others
- 📊 Displays real-time file counts
- 🕒 Live digital clock UI
- 📄 Documentation button (quick access)
- 🎯 Clean and modern GUI design

---
## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python 3.x
- Tkinter (GUI)
- PIL (Pillow)
- OS Module
- Shutil Module

---
## ⚙️ How It Works

1. User selects a folder using the **Browse** button  
2. Application scans all files  
3. Files are categorized based on extensions  
4. Folders are created automatically (if not exist)  
5. Files are moved into respective folders  

---
## 💻 Installation

1. Clone the repository:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/file-sorting-app.git
2. Navigate to project folder: 
cd file-sorting-app

3. Install dependencies:
pip install pillow

4.Run the application: 
python Sorting_app2.py

📂 Supported File Types
| Category  | Extensions                      |
| --------- | ------------------------------- |
| Images    | .jpg, .png, .jpeg               |
| Videos    | .mp4, .avi, .3gp                |
| Audio     | .mp3, .wav                      |
| Documents | .pdf, .docx, .xlsx, .pptx, .txt |
| Others    | Any unsupported files           |

